  Static framework overlay. Values below are taken from ADVAN STOCK, not
  from any running third-party ROM (a running device is a source of
  hardware facts, never of framework config):
    vendor/overlay/FrameworkResOverlay.apk + FrameworkResOverlayExt.apk
    (ADVAN_6781_S34NF2_V4.0_20250304, decoded 2026-09-19 via aapt2).

  DELIBERATELY NOT carried (each with a reason, so nobody re-adds them):
  - config_pri_auto_brightness_* / config_pri_hbm_* (18 arrays): MTK-framework
    names with no AOSP equivalent - an overlay entry for an unknown resource
    fails the build. The AOSP auto-brightness pair below covers the framework.
  - rounded corners: stock sets none (no corner config in either RRO), so the
    AOSP default applies. Do not invent a radius.
  - xml/irq_device_map.xml: MTK-only name, same reason as pri_*.
  - xml/power_profile.xml: staged separately (see below), not inlined here.

  [C] refresh rates: stock declares defaultPeak 120 while the dtb panel
  driver names a 60 Hz mode (Qnt36672e_fhdp_dsi_vdo_60hz). Both are recorded;
  the tester gate (dumpsys display: advertised modes) decides whether 120 is
  real or aspirational. An inherited-AOSP-default defect class lives exactly
  here (RS4: 60 Hz clamp on a 120 Hz panel), so this is verified, not assumed.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- Biometric sensors. AOSP ships this EMPTY with the answer in a
         comment - every device declares its own, or Settings hides
         enrolment and dumpsys reports the wrong modality (RS4: modality 8
         FACE with no fingerprint sensor at all). Stock: exactly one
         fingerprint sensor, no face ("0:2:15"). Matches the Goodix GF3976. -->
    <string-array name="config_biometric_sensors" translatable="false">
        <item>0:2:15</item>
    </string-array>

